The goal of this project is to demonstrate the use of C# programming with delegates concept, windows form, user input, and
calculation. The programmer organized under "GROUP_1X" namespace and the project was designed for our project only(which is
"Student Grade Calculator"). The application is to allow a user to enter student's name and three grade corresponding to Event1,
Event2, Event3, then calculates the student's grade while identifying the lowest and highest grades and determine whether it's
"Passed" or "Failed". During the process of our project, the programmer first put the basic components that users could 
interact with. A "Label" and "TextBox" which created for Event1, Event2, and Event3 which this component where the grade could
be enter. The calculator button was positioned below the input fields and was give a name in to "btnCalculate" so that the 
calculation process will begin whenever the user clicked the button.

The programmer apply the calculation code in "Form1.cs". Before used the mathematical operations, the code checks whether the 
input value enter in the three(3) grade field (Event1, Event2, Event3) that can be conver in to numerical value using 
"double.TryParse", if its invalid the number the compile shows the message "Please enter valid grades". The programmer added a 
second layer which in each grade falls outside the allowed range, the program display the message "Grade must be between 0 and
100".

Once the valid number, the program stores them in an array name "grades". Out programmer initializes the "total" variable to
calculate the value of the grade and start the "lowest" and "highest" variable using the variable in array. Our programmer 
use "foreach" loop to process every grade to the total and compare the current grade with the lowest value either highest
value(if the high number is foud). After the process of grades, our project-application calculates the student's average then
dividing the total grades by the number in array which it has been stored. The delegate named "GradeCalculatorHandler" which
handles the average, lowest, grade, and highest grade as parameters. The "GradeCalculator" event connect it to 
"DisplayResults" method for presenting the calculated information from the user. After that it will determine the student's
status, if the average is 75 or higher the application diplay "Result: PASSED" and if its below 75, the application display
"Result:FAILED" 
